  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Mahesana?", answer: "Send IB Gram your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and we shortlist tutors who teach that exact course. No school in Mahesana district runs the Diploma, MYP or PYP, so matching follows syllabus fit across India instead of location, and lesson times are fitted to your household afterwards. A free trial comes before any decision, and we suggest another tutor if the fit is off." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Mahesana for Cambridge?", answer: "Yes. Tutors for Mahesana teach the Cambridge syllabus as online tuition, not home visits, mirroring what runs at the confirmed schools nearest the city in Ahmedabad, Kalol and Vadodara. Matching is by exact code and tier, commonly Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, using Cambridge's real past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Mahesana?", answer: "No. Tutors do not visit homes in Mahesana. In-person tuition exists only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and everywhere else in India, Mahesana included, lessons run live online and one to one over video with a shared whiteboard. It is online tuition from home, not a tutor turning up at your door." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Mahesana cost?", answer: "The fee reflects programme and level, subject, session length and how recently the tutor taught that syllabus, and we confirm it for your match before the trial. IB Diploma HL subjects usually cost more than Cambridge IGCSE Core help. Sessions are online, so there is no travel element, and no long contract prevents you pausing or stopping." },
    { question: "Which schools near Mahesana offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None inside Mahesana city or district currently holds IB or Cambridge authorisation. The nearest confirmed schools are Mahatma Gandhi International School and Ahmedabad International School in Ahmedabad, about 75 kilometres south, Swayam Cambridge International School at Kalol in Gandhinagar district, and Navrachana International School in Vadodara, Gujarat's only full IB continuum campus." },
    { question: "My child boards at an IB or Cambridge school outside Mahesana. Can a tutor help during holidays?", answer: "Yes, and it is a frequent request from Mahesana, since no local school teaches an international curriculum. We match a tutor to the exact subject, level and syllabus your child's school follows, with lessons scheduled in the holidays or, where the school permits, in agreed evening slots during term." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Yes, each match begins with a free trial class. Your child works a real topic from their syllabus with the tutor online, at no cost and with no duty to continue. A short first-month plan follows, and you can proceed, request changes or try a different tutor." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a child connected to Mahesana?", answer: "Yes, but only as a guide, never as a writer. A tutor can help choose a workable research question, explain what each criterion rewards, plan data collection and give honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting assessed work breaks IB academic integrity rules, so our tutors refuse such requests outright." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Mahesana family?", answer: "We cover nearly every Diploma subject group relevant to a boarding student from Mahesana: Maths Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Mahesana, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the whole IB continuum is covered for Mahesana households whose child attends school elsewhere or is switching curricula after a move back to India. MYP lessons centre on criterion-based analysis in sciences and languages and on the Personal Project journal; PYP lessons cover reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research skills." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students from Mahesana?", answer: "It works well here, given how few local specialists exist for HL subjects or particular Cambridge codes and that the district has no IB or Cambridge school at all. A shared whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked solutions cover nearly all a tutor beside your child would do, while opening the choice of tutor to all of India." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Mahesana students?", answer: "Before any introduction, every tutor is checked on qualifications, recent teaching of the exact subject and level, and their approach to assessment criteria. Because Mahesana has no local IB or Cambridge school, we look especially for tutors who taught that syllabus lately rather than generalists. The free trial class lets you judge the fit yourself." },
    { question: "When should my child connected to Mahesana start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "The ideal point is the start of the course, Class 11 for the IB Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge IGCSE, leaving time to mend foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades pile up together. Final-year starters can still improve, with lessons on the highest-value topics and past papers before the series." },
    { question: "My child is switching from GSEB or CBSE to IGCSE after a move away from Mahesana. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and it is a common request, since several Mahesana families move a child to a Cambridge or IB school in Ahmedabad or Vadodara around Grade 9. The gap is usually question style, not content: command words such as 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, ideally beginning a term before the move." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours for a Mahesana household?", answer: "Yes, most families choose weekday evenings after school plus weekend mornings. We allow for Mahesana's summer heat, when earlier evenings are usually preferred, and for Navratri and Uttarayan, when routines shift for a few days each year. A second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is quick to arrange online." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor matched for our Mahesana family?", answer: "Tell us and we find a different tutor. We review progress every few weeks and offer a re-match whenever the fit is wrong, so a child is never expected to stay with someone who is not working. With no long contract, pausing or stopping sessions carries no penalty." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school near Mahesana or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring platform, with no affiliation to, endorsement from or representation of Mahatma Gandhi International School, Ahmedabad International School, Swayam Cambridge International School, Navrachana International School, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. School names appear only to describe the nearest genuine options for a Mahesana household, and tutors follow each school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

